---
title: "Session host: one channel across dcserver restarts, host loss and terminate"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Termination
    lg1: Session
    lg2: Breaks NoOrphanAfterTerminate or NoSessionLoss
    lg3: Path to the NoOrphanAfterTerminate or NoSessionLoss bug
  }
  class lg0 pink
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 breaks
  class lg3 bugPath
  s0: No session
  s1: No session, a message waiting
  s2: Creating, a message waiting
  s3: Created, location not yet recorded, a message waiting
  s4: Pane recorded, only a shell, a message waiting
  s5: Pane recorded, provider up with its source, not bound, a message waiting
  s6: Session up
  s7: End requested, provider running
  s8: Closing the session
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: a message arrives
  s1 --> s2: a message reserves a new execution
  s2 --> s3: the host creates it
  s3 --> s4: its pane is recorded
  s4 --> s5: the provider starts in the pane
  s5 --> s6: the turn binds the execution
  s6 --> s6: a host probe stops failing
  s6 --> s7: an end is requested
  s7 --> s8: the close is sent
  classDef breaks fill:#ffecee,stroke:#e72e3b,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#cd2834
  class s0 teal
  class s0 bugPath
  class s1 teal
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 teal
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 teal
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 teal
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 teal
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 teal
  class s6 bugPath
  class s7 pink
  class s7 bugPath
  class s8 pink
  class s8 breaks
  class s8 bugPath
